    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and all its tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an optional 4-digit `postcode` to owners, validated per the city's region on create.\n\n**New, self-contained units (no surrounding complexity to hold):**\n- `RequirePostcode.java` \u2014 one function: skips when absent, else requires 4 digits and, for a city with a known region (via the existing `Locality.of(city)` helper), enforces NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099. Unknown regions accept any 4-digit code.\n- `InvalidPostcodeException.java` (checked) + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` (responds 400), mirroring the existing escalation pattern.\n- Escalation YAML wiring the handler.\n\n**Small edits to existing files:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `postcode` step after `validate` (which already publishes the request body as a variable).\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `postcode` field plus a getter/setter (MapStruct maps it automatically in/out, so the mapper was untouched).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema so the generated DTO carries it in requests and responses.\n- hsqldb `schema.sql` / `data.sql` \u2014 added the `postcode` column at the end of `owners` and a trailing `NULL` to the positional seed inserts (matching how the earlier columns like `customer_code`/`namesake_count` were added only to the hsqldb profile used by the tests).\n\nI kept each changed function trivial (CC ~1, small edits) and added behaviour as new cohesive classes rather than growing `RequireOwnerFields`, `BuildOwner`, or the mapper.\n\nResults: `Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the full suite (the only test class, `AcceptanceTest`) is green: valid postcode stored/returned, owner without postcode accepted, malformed postcode rejected with 400.",
